- If the tree is empty, return false.
- Check whether the current node is a leaf.
- If it is a leaf, compare its value with the remaining sum.
- Subtract the current nodes value from `targetSum`.
- Check the left and right subtrees.
- If at least one path matches, return true.
Time Complexity: O(n)

In the worst case, all nodes in the tree must be checked if no suitable path exists.

Space Complexity: O(h) — the maximum depth of the recursion stack.
 An iterative DFS using a stack could be used, but the time complexity would remain O(n).
